  "finalText": "All 14 tickets in the new queue were triaged, according to the worker's report. I have no tools here, so everything below comes from that report and I haven't checked it independently.\n\n**Merged duplicates**\n- T-2005 was merged into T-2004 (CRM search), the earliest report.\n- T-2012 was merged into T-2003 (payments builds), also the earliest report.\n- Neither set had a deadline before triage, so both survivors got 12:10 UTC.\n- The report doesn't say whether references to the merged tickets were moved to the survivors, as the handbook requires.\n\n**Closed as not service requests**\n- T-2010 is SyncFlow marketing.\n- T-2014 is an out-of-office auto-reply.\n\n**Triaged tickets** (all ten are now open; severity from the matrix, assignee on call when the deadline falls)\n\n| Ticket | Sev | Due (UTC) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2003 Payments builds | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-101 Dana Whitfield (platform-primary) |\n| T-2004 CRM search | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac (business-apps) |\n| T-2013 Lisbon VPN | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen (network-secondary) |\n| T-2006 Payslip tax code | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2011 Overtime import | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2007 Phishing report | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-601 Noor Haddad (security-oncall) |\n| T-2001 Berlin VPN | sev3 | 03-23 17:00 | E-303 |\n| T-2002 CRM filter | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-203 Amara Osei (business-apps-secondary) |\n| T-2008 VPN client update | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-302 Marcus Feld (network-primary) |\n| T-2009 Build logs slow | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-102 Ravi Menon (platform-primary) |\n\n**Reasoning the worker gave**\n- **T-2006:** The matrix alone would make it sev3, but KB-55 amends it to sev2 for 03-20 to 03-31 (payroll close).\n- **T-2007:** It is a phishing report, so it is a security incident: sev2, owned by security-oncall rather than the VPN rotation.\n- **Sev1/sev2 deadlines:** These run on the clock, 240 minutes from 08:10, which gives 12:10.\n- **Sev3/sev4 deadlines:** These count business hours only, starting when the desk opens at 09:00. T-2001 is due Monday 17:00. The sev4 tickets are due Thursday 03-26 at 17:00, because Wednesday 03-25 is a company holiday.\n- **Leave cover:** E-301 (network-primary) is on leave today, so network tickets due today went to network-secondary (E-303). E-202 (business-apps) is on leave 03-26, so T-2002 went to business-apps-secondary (E-203).\n\n**Not done**\n- No escalations or pages were made. The worker judged that triage didn't call for them.\n- No major-incident runbook was run. The worker found nothing company-wide, though it flagged the Lisbon VPN and CRM (Sales) outages as department-level issues to watch.\n- The sev2 tickets due at 12:10 are the ones to watch: T-2003, T-2004, T-2013 and T-2007.",
